PROPOSED — NOT FINAL. Jeff writes the licence text; this states the intent so
the repository is not published without one.

Three different things are in here and they do not want the same terms:

1. THE CODE AND THE STYLESHEET (chrome.js, assets/brand.css, test/)
   Proposed: MIT. Nothing in them is a competitive asset, and a permissive
   licence is what makes the repository safe to make public so the Lightsail
   box can install it without credentials.

2. THE FONTS (assets/fonts/)
   Not GateIron's to license. Fraunces and Hanken Grotesk are under the SIL
   Open Font License 1.1, which permits bundling and redistribution provided
   the licence travels with them and they are not sold on their own. Both
   texts are in that directory and must stay there.

3. THE GATE MARK (assets/gate-dark.png, assets/gate-light.png) AND THE NAME
   GateIron, LLC's. Publishing the files in a public repository is not a
   grant of permission to use the mark or the name. Proposed wording: "The
   GateIron name and the gate mark are trademarks of GateIron, LLC. No licence
   to use them is granted by this repository."

   Worth Jeff's decision rather than mine: the mark is already downloadable
   from gateiron.com, so a public repository reveals nothing new. If he would
   rather it not ship here at all, the package can take the mark as a consumer
   supplied asset instead - the only code change is that gateMark() reads a
   path from the assets option.
